Z||000000||Simple Fiero||07-14-2001||07:31 PM||||Yesterday I took my dash apart, to see if there were any volts to my gas gauge cause it has not been working. When I got the dash off I noticed that there was a piece of paper stuck behind the gauge needle, so I pulled it off, reset the needle and turned it to the on position, still nothing, so I thought (stupidly) I will start it maybe that will work, suddenly the car would turn over but not start. So My father and I took off the air cleaner to see if it was getting any gas and guess what no gas. So I thought great now the fuel pump is taken a dump. So I called BCAA that was 40 bucks. Canadian Tire told me they could fix it ( I am just learning mechanical know how and have no idea how to do this yet) It started out at 50 bucks for the inspection to see what the real problem is. Turned out I was right it was the fuel pump so that is 60 bucks, so now I am mad but not flaming mad. So I get a phone call this morning, and it turns out the previous owner, screwed up the previous installation of the pump and just soldered the wiring harnass on. SO that wiring thingy was another 50 from pontiac. I finally get the bill and it was 450 dollars. So I am out 500 dollars for all this trouble. and my gas gauge still doesn't work and now I have to park my car so  I can afford to live. (Now I don't make very much money, and luckily I got paid my mid month cheque which I now only have a 100 to my name.) But I keep telling myself that I am going to make and I am going to that is for sure, some how!<BR>Sorry for this little bit of rambling but I do have a technical question, (for the canadian boys out there, or anybody else) how much is it to replace the clutch (someone told me it was over 1000 dollars) and is it hard to do yourself. Also my fan never works I am wondering if it is a fan motor, funny thing is my temp gauge never gets over 60 or 70. So maybe it is a termostat or a sensor, could someone help me with this silly stuff<P>88SC<BR>White<BR>98,000 kms<BR>2.5L<p>[This message has been edited by Simple Fiero (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||07-14-2001||07:45 PM||||Hey Simple Fiero!<BR>  Get a manual from Hanes if you can...<BR>It should answer most of your questions in a straight forward way...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||07-14-2001||08:40 PM||||A clutch job can run $800-1200USD.  It's a big job, but not out of line for a do-it-yourselfer if you have a garage, 2 floor jacks, some jack stands, and a good set of tools.  Oh, yeah, and a friend helps too.  I did the clutch in my Fiero right after buying it.  If we worked straight through, it would have taken about 16-20 hours total labor.  I could do it again in about 10-12 (frozen bolts not withstanding).  Ed Park's Fiero Factory has info on how to swap the clutch yourself without having to pull the motor.  You will have to drop on end of the cradle though, and take the tranny out through the wheel well.  Good luck!||||reg||10
Z||000003||ArchMagi||07-14-2001||11:16 PM||||Yeah! another BC member!<P>Simple, welcome!<P>The woman who had my 87 before i did had the clutch replaced about 1 1/2 years ago and it was approx 838.23$ canadian.  Thats parts and labour.  If your going to replace the clutch yourself iv herd that the easiest way is to drop the entire cradel.<P>My temp is around 70-75 average.  Hot day or stop and go traffic, maybe in the 90 range.<P>As for your gas gauge, i have no clue, sorry.<P>------------------<BR>-------------------------<BR>1987 Fiero||||reg||1
